0Basidiocarp usually omphalioid, sometimes more tricholomatoid; pileus hygrophanous or not, trans1ucently striate or not; lamellae usually decurrent, sometimes broadly adnate; stipe centrally inserted; spore print white, whitish, pale cream, ochraceous, or pinkish to orange-tinged cream.  Spores smooth, thin- to somewhat thick-walled, non-amyloid, cyanophilous or not; basidia almost always 4-spored; lamella edge fertile, almost always without cheilocystidia, but often with undifferentiated cystidio1es or basidio1es; pleurocystidia absent; pileipellis a cutis of parallel to partIy ascending hyphae; pigment intrace llular, membranal, or incrusting; hymeno¬phoral trama usually regu1ar, but irregu1ar towards subhymenium, rare1y subirregular; clamp-connections almost always present. - Lectotype species: C nebularis (Batsch: Fr.) Kumm. 050172770_Note0
